  # ============ real Accela sandbox ============
  # create_inspection_checklists/create_inspection_conditions and friends are
  # now granted (see ACCELA_CONSTRUCT_SCOPE), so these reach Accela for
  # real - but each one still fails, for reasons that are Accela's own
  # behavior rather than a missing scope or a bug in this module:
  # - checklists/create: 500 - a bare {"name": ...} isn't a complete
  #   checklist payload for this agency/inspection type (Accela's real
  #   checklist schema needs checklist items, which is beyond this
  #   module's/this test's scope to construct); since nothing gets
  #   created, checklists/delete on any id then gets a 403 rather than a
  #   404 - Accela's own "nothing to operate on" response here, not a
  #   scope gap.
  # - conditions/create: the same "Request body is required" quirk
  #   documented on records/conditions/create and inspections/related/
  #   create - occurs regardless of payload shape.
  # - conditions/update and conditions/delete, given a condition id that
  #   was never created, get a clean real 404 instead.

  assign real_fixture_record = { "type": { "id": "Building-Home.cOccupation-NA-NA" }, "description": "pos-module-accela_construct test fixture (inspections_checklists_conditions_test)" }
  function real_create_result = 'modules/accela_construct/commands/records/create', record: real_fixture_record
